  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 201 PM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nThe cool Canadian high pressure will be moving to the south and east \nof the region starting Sunday. This large synoptic movement will \nbring in a prolonged period of south to southwest winds to the \nregion, and with that, temperatures rising back above normal through \nmost of the week ahead. \n\nThis rather high confidence warmer than normal has been supported by \nCPC outlooks for several days, and might appear to some as another \nwave of heat, but in this case, we're looking at pleasant weather, \nwith highs in the 70s, and lows in the 40s and 50s. \n\nAny cloud cover or precipitation chances remain silent in the week \nahead, as an upper ridge builds aloft mid week.  Once that pattern \nbreaks down, which may not be until the weekend or beyond, dry \nweather should be the dominant feature of the forecast.",
